  "latest_changes": [
    "Direct-script startup, normal shutdown, dual-axis gyroscopic rings, and finite vent cycle; no Animation Engine dependency",
    "103 active subparts: 4 rings, 4 floor leaves, 80 tiles, plasma, 6 shield sleeves, 4 roof leaves and 4 inner ceiling leaves; obsolete 32 intake vane dummies removed",
    "Paired four-leaf doors, 3.72m visual bore and lined connecting tube/pockets; centred top conveyor connection retained under custom hatch",
    "Separate saved/synced gyro phases, perpendicular axes, distinct secondary rates and smooth two-axis shutdown braking",
    "10-second output ramp after completed assembly; normal shutdown holds containment until heat <=15%, then brakes and dismantles",
    "Actual fuel tiers I/II/III with native-conveyor inventory transfers and 10 GW / 100 GW / 1 TW rated outputs",
    "Vent cuts power after shield closure, ejects containment and deployed rings, purges heat, closes and stays off until manual restart",
    "Vent damage uses captured load and heat: reactor 1-15%, attached compatible modules 2-20% of maximum integrity, once per loaded vent",
    "Neon emissives at 4x intensity; vent and incomplete pulse red/black, off red, starvation yellow, active fuel-tier colours",
    "Load-scaled core bob/drift and irregular rotation; primary ring baseline 3x original, up to9x at full load",
    "Sphere construction tier speeds 1x/1.5x/2x; mechanical sequences retain original timings",
    "Glass baseline haze: ColorAdd RGBA .008/.009/.010/.025; existing native dirt and reflection settings retained",
    "3x1x3 vent duct/outlet models and definitions; synchronized four-leaf outlet door with emissives",
    "Selected 1.6m x1.0m standard/advanced piggyback packs with native upgrade detectors and 2.3m reactor socket surrounds",
    "Thick triangular containment component, assembler recipe and five model-rendered icons",
    "80 installed tiles reserved at startup, retained through shutdown, four-item maintenance batches dependent on tier/load/heat, consumed field discarded on vent; authoritative state saved/synced",
    "Low-load spectator recordings of preceding reactor revision completed; reactor and both controllers repaired and verified after reload/resave",
    "Native power sinks on physical containment controllers; adaptable priority-2 containment group",
    "1/10/100MW upkeep, 90-second grid-charged shutdown reserve; startup waits for full precharge; blackout initiates shutdown, exhausted reserve pauses mechanisms",
    "Explicit inventory whitelist and empty-slot tooltip accept Fuel I/II/III and containment tiles on server and clients",
    "Saved/synced quartet maintenance launches from fixed dispensers into moving shell; normal shutdown completes an active replacement",
    "Terminal power, reserve time, loose tile stock, restart shortfall and maintenance endurance information",
    "Containment rotational amplitude raised from 0.75 to 6 degrees at idle, reaching 9.25 degrees at full load; translational wiggle/bob, motion frequencies and gyro rings unchanged.",
    "Core now tumbles with slow continuous yaw/roll spin, broad unequal direction-reversing sweeps and smaller tilt adjustments. Reuses synchronized load-driven phase; brakes and realigns before dismantling. Positional wiggle/bob and rings unchanged.",
    "Shared emissive intensity increased from4 to12 for reactor/subparts and vent outlet. One client-only 4.5m shadowless core light follows visible plasma, fuel/alarm colour, vent pulse and shutdown/ejection fades; removed on Close.",
    "Heat-squared tile wear; exhausted replacement quartet limits output to 10% of captured load and raises burn to 10x that load.",
    "125% supercritical threshold, irreversible saved fuse accelerated by peak heat; 5/20/100x large-warhead damage with cube-root radius.",
    "Scripted launch hands off beyond outlet to physical spent rings/tiles and a physical plasma carrier; gravity and randomized launch/spin.",
    "Generated fuel-tinted plasma texture, smooth sphere, open thick tile frames; seven freshly exported MWM/HKT models.",
